@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s342e-several-employers`

-- TESTS for the several-employers regulations of 5757-1997 (row IL-34, priorities 2 and 3). Every expected value was worked out by
-- hand from the Hebrew text before the run; the arithmetic is beside each group. The full rate used throughout is 0.07 (an
-- input: the 7% of the Schedule J deduction column above the reduced collection threshold that row IL-05's tests use).

§ `Tests: the several-employers regulations`

§§ `Fixtures`

`a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 July 2026` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 7 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 March 2026` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 April 2026` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 4 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 June 2026` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 August 2026` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 8 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 from only some employers` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS FALSE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 without the wage` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS FALSE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS TRUE
`a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 without the rate` MEANS `A wage certificate under regulation 3A` WITH
    `the day it was delivered` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `it is from each of the employee's other employers` IS TRUE,
    `it details the wage paid in the month before the day it was delivered` IS TRUE, `it states the rate of contributions deducted` IS FALSE

`a complete refund request` MEANS `A refund request under regulation 3C` WITH
    `it is on the Institute's form` IS TRUE, `it has a certificate from each of the employee's employers` IS TRUE,
    `each certificate gives the monthly wage, the period of the wage and the sums deducted` IS TRUE
`a refund request not on the Institute's form` MEANS `A refund request under regulation 3C` WITH
    `it is on the Institute's form` IS FALSE, `it has a certificate from each of the employee's employers` IS TRUE,
    `each certificate gives the monthly wage, the period of the wage and the sums deducted` IS TRUE
`a refund request missing a certificate` MEANS `A refund request under regulation 3C` WITH
    `it is on the Institute's form` IS TRUE, `it has a certificate from each of the employee's employers` IS FALSE,
    `each certificate gives the monthly wage, the period of the wage and the sums deducted` IS TRUE
`a refund request whose certificates lack the sums` MEANS `A refund request under regulation 3C` WITH
    `it is on the Institute's form` IS TRUE, `it has a certificate from each of the employee's employers` IS TRUE,
    `each certificate gives the monthly wage, the period of the wage and the sums deducted` IS FALSE

§§ `Regulation 8: from 1 March 1997`

#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — the day from which regulations 2 and 3 apply` EQUALS YMD 1997 3 1
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — regulations 2 and 3 apply to a monthly income paid for the day` (YMD 1997 3 1)
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — regulations 2 and 3 apply to a monthly income paid for the day` (YMD 2026 10 9)
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — regulations 2 and 3 apply to a monthly income paid for the day` (YMD 1997 2 28)

§§ `Regulation 9: five months, five equal parts`

-- July to November 1997 is five months; 1,000 / 5 = 200; 1,234.50 / 5 = 246.90.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the month is one of the five months of the transition` 1997 `,` 7
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the month is one of the five months of the transition` 1997 `,` 11
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the month is one of the five months of the transition` 1997 `,` 6
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the month is one of the five months of the transition` 1997 `,` 12
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the month is one of the five months of the transition` 1998 `,` 7
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the equal part deducted in each of the five months` 1_000 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the equal part deducted in each of the five months` 1_234.50 EQUALS 246.9

§§ `Regulation 2: the employer reached, and the deduction`

#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — the regulation reaches an employer:` TRUE  `, or one to whom` FALSE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — the regulation reaches an employer:` FALSE `, or one to whom` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — the regulation reaches an employer:` TRUE  `, or one to whom` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — the regulation reaches an employer:` FALSE `, or one to whom` FALSE
-- A wage of 10,000 at the full rate 0.07, on the whole wage: 700. A wage of 0: 0.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — where` TRUE `, the deduction from a wage of` 10_000 `at the full rate` 0.07 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — where` TRUE `, the deduction from a wage of` 0 `at the full rate` 0.07 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — where` FALSE `, the deduction from a wage of` 10_000 `at the full rate` 0.07 BECAUSE "regulation 2 does not reach this employer, whose deduction is section 342(c)'s (row IL-05)"

§§ `Regulation 2A: the form`

#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the employee is bound to fill in the Institute's form` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the employee is bound to fill in the Institute's form` FALSE
-- Handed over on 5 January, wage received on 10 January: before it; at the start of the tax year: yes.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the form was handed over in time:` (YMD 2026 1 5) `, the wage received on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, at the start of the tax year being` TRUE
-- The same day is not "before"; one day after is not before; the second limb missing is not in time.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the form was handed over in time:` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, the wage received on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, at the start of the tax year being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the form was handed over in time:` (YMD 2026 1 11) `, the wage received on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, at the start of the tax year being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the form was handed over in time:` (YMD 2026 1 5) `, the wage received on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, at the start of the tax year being` FALSE

§§ `Regulation 3(a): the collection clerk`

-- Total income 20,000 at 0.07 = 1,400 under reg 2. Coordinated contributions 1,200: 1,400 exceeds them: the clerk may (proved).
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3(a) — the clerk may give the employee a certificate: total income` 20_000 `, full rate` 0.07 `, coordinated contributions` 1_200 `, proved to the clerk's satisfaction being` TRUE
-- 1,400 does not exceed 1,400; nor 1,500.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3(a) — the clerk may give the employee a certificate: total income` 20_000 `, full rate` 0.07 `, coordinated contributions` 1_400 `, proved to the clerk's satisfaction being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3(a) — the clerk may give the employee a certificate: total income` 20_000 `, full rate` 0.07 `, coordinated contributions` 1_500 `, proved to the clerk's satisfaction being` TRUE
-- Not proved: no.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3(a) — the clerk may give the employee a certificate: total income` 20_000 `, full rate` 0.07 `, coordinated contributions` 1_200 `, proved to the clerk's satisfaction being` FALSE

§§ `Regulation 3A(a): the secondary employer's sum (fork N1)`

-- Coordinated 1,000, the others deducted 600: 400. Others 1,000: 0 (no refusal at zero).
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, the others having deducted` 600 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, the others having deducted` 1_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, the others having deducted` 0 EQUALS 1_000
-- The others deducted MORE (1,200 against 1,000): declined at the switch; 0 at the other named reading.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, the others having deducted` 1_200 BECAUSE "regulation 3A(a) does not say what the secondary employer deducts when the other employers have already deducted more than the coordinated contributions"
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, the others having deducted` 1_200 `, reading a negative difference as` `a negative difference leaves nothing for the secondary employer to deduct` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, the others having deducted` 1_200 `, reading a negative difference as` `a negative difference is declined` BECAUSE "regulation 3A(a) does not say what the secondary employer deducts when the other employers have already deducted more than the coordinated contributions"
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the reading this row takes of a negative difference` EQUALS `a negative difference is declined`

§§ `Regulation 3A(d): what a wage certificate is`

#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) — it is a wage certificate` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) — it is a wage certificate` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 from only some employers`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) — it is a wage certificate` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 without the wage`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(d) — it is a wage certificate` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 without the rate`

§§ `Regulation 3A(b) and (c): the months`

-- (b): a certificate on 1 January covers January to June; one on 1 July covers July to December. The employee began in 2025.
#ASSERT     `the day the wage certificate of the half of the year holding month` 1 `of` 2026 `is due under reg 3A(b)` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT     `the day the wage certificate of the half of the year holding month` 6 `of` 2026 `is due under reg 3A(b)` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT     `the day the wage certificate of the half of the year holding month` 7 `of` 2026 `is due under reg 3A(b)` EQUALS YMD 2026 7 1
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 1 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 July 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 12 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 July 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 July 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- Not worked in the month; a defective certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 from only some employers` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026 without the wage` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- (c): began 15 March 2026, certificate on 1 March: March to June, not February, not July.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 March 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 March 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 March 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 March 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- A certificate on 1 April is not "at the beginning of the month in which he began" (March).
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 4 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 April 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- Began 2 January, certificate 1 January: after 1 January, at the beginning of January: January to June.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 1 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 1 2) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- Second half: began 15 August, certificate 1 August: August to December, not July.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 8 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 August 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 8 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 12 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 August 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 8 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 August 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 8 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- Began 20 June, certificate 1 June: June only (the first half ends).
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 June 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 6 20) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 June 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 6 20) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- A start in an earlier year is not a start "in the half": a certificate on 1 August 2026 does not serve a man who began on 15 August 2025.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 8 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 August 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 8 15) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- Months out of range.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 0 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 13 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `a wage certificate dated 1 July 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"

§§ `Regulations 3B and 3C`

#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B — reg 3A applies: employer reached by reg 2 being` TRUE `, recognised being` TRUE `, details given being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B — reg 3A applies: employer reached by reg 2 being` TRUE `, recognised being` TRUE `, details given being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B — reg 3A applies: employer reached by reg 2 being` TRUE `, recognised being` FALSE `, details given being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B — reg 3A applies: employer reached by reg 2 being` FALSE `, recognised being` FALSE `, details given being` TRUE
-- 3C: 1,200 deducted against 1,000 coordinated, a complete request: yes. Equal: no. Each flaw: no.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C — a complete request for a refund: deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, request` `a complete refund request`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C — a complete request for a refund: deducted` 1_000 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, request` `a complete refund request`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C — a complete request for a refund: deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, request` `a refund request not on the Institute's form`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C — a complete request for a refund: deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, request` `a refund request missing a certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C — a complete request for a refund: deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, request` `a refund request whose certificates lack the sums`

§§ `Regulation 4: the account`

-- 52,000 exceeds the maximum 51,910 (the Institute's published 2026 figure that row IL-05 carries): with a certificate, or a 3A deduction: must file.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 52_000 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` TRUE `, deduction under reg 3A being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 52_000 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` FALSE `, deduction under reg 3A being` TRUE
-- Equal to the maximum is not "exceeding"; no certificate and no 3A deduction is not a duty.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 51_910 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` TRUE `, deduction under reg 3A being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 60_000 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` FALSE `, deduction under reg 3A being` FALSE
-- Due by 31 July of the following year.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the day by which the account is due, for the tax year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2027 7 31
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the day by which the account is due, for the tax year` 2025 EQUALS YMD 2026 7 31

§§ `Regulation 5: the employee pays the difference`

#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 5 — the difference the employee pays: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, actual deduction` 600 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 5 — the difference the employee pays: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, actual deduction` 1_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 5 — the difference the employee pays: coordinated contributions` 1_000 `, actual deduction` 1_100 EQUALS 0

§§ `Regulation 6: the refund`

-- The tax year 2018 ends on 31.12.2018; seven years on is 31.12.2025.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the last day to file the account for the tax year` 2018 EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the last day to file the account for the tax year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2033 12 31
-- Filed on the last day: deducted 1,200 against 1,000: 200. A day later: declined by name. Under-deducted: 0.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the refund for a month of the tax year` 2018 `, the account filed on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the refund for a month of the tax year` 2018 `, the account filed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 BECAUSE "regulation 6(a) refunds on an account filed within seven years of the end of the tax year and does not say what follows a later account"
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the refund for a month of the tax year` 2018 `, the account filed on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, deducted` 900 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the refund for a month of the tax year` 2026 `, the account filed on` (YMD 2026 10 9) `, deducted` 1_050.5 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 EQUALS 50.5
-- (b): three months from receipt: 31 January + 3 months clamps to 30 April; 9 October 2026 + 3 months is 9 January 2027.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) — the day by which the refund is due: request received` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, doubt being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) — the day by which the refund is due: request received` (YMD 2026 10 9) `, doubt being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2027 1 9
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) — the day by which the refund is due: request received` (YMD 2026 10 9) `, doubt being` TRUE BECAUSE "regulation 6(b) lets the Institute delay the refund until its doubt is cleared, so no day is due"

§§ `Regulation 7: linkage`

-- (1): the 15th of the month after: March 2026 -> 15 April 2026; January -> 15 February; December 2026 -> 15 January 2027.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) — the day the excess is taken to have been paid, before any move under s 353(b), for month` 3 `of` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 15
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) — the day the excess is taken to have been paid, before any move under s 353(b), for month` 1 `of` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) — the day the excess is taken to have been paid, before any move under s 353(b), for month` 12 `of` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2027 1 15
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) — the day the excess is taken to have been paid, before any move under s 353(b), for month` 0 `of` 2026 BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
-- (2): 1,000 x (102.5 / 100 - 1) = 25; no change in the index: 0.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` 1_000 `, the index being` 100 `then and` 102.5 `at the refund` EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` 1_000 `, the index being` 100 `then and` 100 `at the refund` EQUALS 0
-- A fall from 100 to 99: declined at the switch; 0 at "no addition"; 1,000 x (99 / 100 - 1) = -10 at "reduces".
#ASSERT REFUSED `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` 1_000 `, the index being` 100 `then and` 99 `at the refund` BECAUSE "section 362(a)(1) adds the rate of rise of the index and says nothing of a fall"
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` 1_000 `, the index being` 100 `then and` 99 `at the refund, reading a fall as` `a fall in the index leaves no addition` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the addition to a refund of` 1_000 `, the index being` 100 `then and` 99 `at the refund, reading a fall as` `a fall in the index reduces the refund by the rate of the fall` EQUALS -10
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(2) — the reading this row takes of a fall in the index` EQUALS `a fall in the index is declined`
